{
  "mn124:0.1": "Middle Discourses 124 ",
  "mn124:0.2": "With Bakkula ",
  "mn124:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn124:1.2": "At one time Venerable Bakkula was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "mn124:2.1": "Then the naked ascetic Kassapa, an old friend of Bakkula in the lay life, approached him, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn124:2.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Venerable Bakkula, ",
  "mn124:3.1": "“Reverend Bakkula, how long has it been since you went forth?” ",
  "mn124:3.2": "“It has been eighty years, reverend.” ",
  "mn124:3.3": "“But in these eighty years, how many times have you had sex?” ",
  "mn124:3.4": "“You shouldn’t ask me such a question. ",
  "mn124:3.5": "",
  "mn124:3.6": "Rather, you should ask me this: ",
  "mn124:3.7": "‘But in these eighty years, how many times have sensual perceptions ever arisen in you?’” ",
  "mn124:3.8": "“But in these eighty years, how many times have sensual perceptions ever arisen in you?” ",
  "mn124:3.9": "“In these eighty years, I don’t recall that any sensual perception has ever arisen in me.” ",
  "mn124:3.10": "This we remember as an incredible and amazing quality of Venerable Bakkula. ",
  "mn124:4-5.1": "“In these eighty years, I don’t recall that any perception of ill will … ",
  "mn124:4-5.2": "or cruelty has ever arisen in me.” ",
  "mn124:4-5.3": "This too we remember as an incredible and ama